Typical daily responsibilities of a Databricks data engineer
Develop PySpark and SQL notebooks for data transformations.
Build and maintain ingestion pipelines from source systems.
Implement Bronze, Silver and Gold Delta tables.
Develop incremental loads and CDC processing.
Create reusable functions and configuration-driven pipelines.
Schedule workflows and configure dependencies.
Validate source-to-target data counts and business rules.
Troubleshoot failed jobs and resolve data quality issues.
Optimize Spark jobs and SQL queries.
Manage code through Git and deploy changes across environments.
Monitor production pipelines and meet SLA requirements.
Coordinate with business analysts, source-system teams and BI developers.

4. Example project workflow
Consider a retail analytics project that loads customer, product, order and sales data from a SQL Server database.
Ingest source data: Load customer, product and sales tables into Databricks.
Create Bronze tables: Store raw records in Delta tables with ingestion timestamps.
Create Silver tables: Remove duplicates, validate customer IDs, handle null values and standardize dates.
Implement incremental loads: Process only new or changed records using watermarks or CDC.
Create Gold tables: Build sales fact tables, customer dimensions and daily sales summaries.
Orchestrate pipelines: Schedule ingestion and transformation jobs with dependencies and retries.
Perform testing: Compare source and target counts, validate totals and check business rules.
Deploy to production: Promote tested code and configure production schedules and alerts.
Support production: Investigate failures, correct data issues and monitor pipeline performance.
Document mappings, architecture, dependencies and operational support



